config UHC_AGM
	bool "AgRV2K USB0 host controller driver"
	depends on DT_HAS_AGM_AGRV2K_UHC_ENABLED
	default y
	help
	  Host-mode driver for the AgRV2K on-die USB0 controller
	  (FSL/ChipIdea-like dual-role silicon driven through its
	  EHCI-compatible operational registers: USBCMD/USBSTS/PORTSC, the
	  asynchronous queue-head ring and the periodic frame list).

	  The device-mode counterpart is UDC_AGM on the agm,agrv2k-usb0 node.
	  USB0 is one piece of silicon with one role at a time, so enable
	  exactly one of the two devicetree nodes (usb0 / uhc0) per build.

	  Full speed only, no high-speed chirp and no isochronous scheduling;
	  control, bulk and interrupt transfers, one root port, no external
	  hubs.
